  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting National Leadership on Durable Solutions and Promoting Local Integration, Voluntary Return, and Social Cohesion in the Central African Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project&apos;s first objective strengthens national leadership and coordination of lasting solutions at all levels, bolstered by data, analysis, and practical tools. The second objective advocates for the sustainable local settlement of internally displaced persons (IDPs) in Bria, granting them rights to housing, land, and property, essential services, and means of livelihood. This approach, which provides concrete aid to vulnerable IDP populations and policy and regulatory support to the government, is endorsed and requested by the authorities. The third objective promotes social unity and peace among IDPs and their host communities. It concentrates on integrating the lasting solutions agenda with broader national policies that foster social unity, including a deeper alliance with MAHRN and the fortification of local peace committees, as part of a nationally driven strategy to cultivate social harmony and peace.</narrative>
  </description>
